  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Soutien multisectoriel aux populations vuln&#xe9;rables d&#xe9;plac&#xe9;es de force et aux communaut&#xe9;s h&#xf4;tes dans les r&#xe9;gions du Nord, du Centre-Nord et de l&#x2019;Est.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide protection, camp coordination and camp management, and shelter and non-food items assistance to vulnerable communities affected by conflict-related displacement in Ouahigouya, Boulsa, Kongoussi, and Bogande. This UNHCR project provides emergency shelter, legal assistance for housing and agriculture lands to both displaced people and members of host communities, and psychosocial support to people in need. The project targets 152,055 people, including 26,552 women, 19,767 men, 70,646 children, and 22,807 persons with disabilities with protection activities. Additionally, over 40,000 people are targeted under the camp coordination and shelter and non-food items sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
